WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.312 --> 00:00:02.789
(bouncy, honking music)

00:00:02.789 --> 00:00:04.370
- [Narrator] Floating markets
have been at the center

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.240
of communities in Thailand
for hundreds of years.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.490
(bouncy, upbeat music)

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.107
They were originally built
along canals and rivers

00:00:15.107 --> 00:00:18.036
at a time when water transport
played an important role

00:00:18.036 --> 00:00:19.767
in daily life.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:21.529
One of the most popular in Thailand

00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:25.809
is the Amphawa Floating
Market, 45 miles from Bangkok.

00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:29.976
It stretches 30 miles along
a canal on the Mekong River.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.390
And today, hundreds of vendors
use the Amphawa Floating

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.942
Market to sell and cook a wide variety

00:00:36.942 --> 00:00:39.025
of delicious Thai dishes.

00:03:07.638 --> 00:03:09.805
(chiming)

